Oka Example: VARCHAR
Definition: VARCHAR stores variable-length character data

Why?
Because names, emails, usernames etc. don't always have the same length

Real-time: Instagram username, customer name, email

Hands-on chyali:
CREATE TABLE users (
    username VARCHAR(50)
);

Interview: Why did you choose VARCHAR instead of CHAR?
Expected thinking: VARCHAR is generally suitable when the stored strings have variable lengths, while CHAR is fixed-length -- That's how you should study every concept

